course: dictionary
lesson: 15037
title: Retailers and shops
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A retailer is a person or business that sells goods to the public. Look for clues like shop, sells, buys and goods. «The retailer put the new toys on the shelves» means the shop had toys ready for people to buy.
explain: Retailers often buy goods from a wholesaler or a factory first. Then they sell the goods to you and add a little extra money, called profit. Profit is what the retailer keeps after paying for the goods.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «You can buy these boots from all good retailers» still makes sense if you think: you can buy these boots from all good shops and stores.
fact: A retailer is a person or business that sells goods to the public.
fact: A retailer can be a shop, a supermarket or an online store.
fact: A retailer usually buys goods from a wholesaler or a factory first.
fact: Retailers add profit to the price, which is the money they keep when they sell.
fact: Small retailers include corner shops; big retailers include supermarkets and department stores.
exercise: «The retailer put the new toys on the shelves.» What is a retailer? | A factory that makes toys | A child who likes to play with toys | *A shop or business that sells goods to the public
exercise: Which of these is a small retailer? | A factory that makes bricks | *A corner shop on your street | A ship that carries goods across the sea
exercise: Mum says, «You can find this juice at all good retailers.» What does retailers mean here? | *Shops and stores that sell to customers | People who grow fruit on farms | Teachers who give lessons about juice
test: «Our online retailer sent the parcel today.» What does online retailer mean? | A person who fixes computers | *A business that sells goods to people over the internet | A game played on a computer
test: A retailer buys goods from a wholesaler and adds profit when selling. Why does a retailer add profit? | *To make money from selling the goods | To give the goods away for free | To make goods cheaper for the factory
exam: Which best explains what a retailer does? | Delivers letters to people's homes | Grows food on a farm | *Sells goods to the public, such as in a shop | Makes goods in a factory
